# plans/plan_dx9.md D9-A5 scene corpus: sprite_mirror_quad
# The second D9-92 scene, proving TextureAddressMode.Mirror is genuinely DIFFERENT from Wrap
# (sprite_wrap_quad.scene), not just "some non-Clamp behavior". Same 2x1 RED/GREEN texture and
# sourceRectangle=(0,0,4,1) (double width) as sprite_wrap_quad.scene, only spritesampler changes
# from PointWrap to a custom Point-filtered Mirror sampler (constructed manually -- real XNA has
# no named "PointMirror" SamplerState preset, only PointClamp/PointWrap/LinearClamp/LinearWrap/
# AnisotropicClamp/AnisotropicWrap).
#
# Standard GPU mirror addressing folds U outside [0,1] as a triangle wave (period 2): for
# u in [1,2], u_effective = 2-u. This gives a SYMMETRIC pattern around the U=1 boundary, NOT
# Wrap's repeating one:
#   U in [0,0.5)   -> texel0 (RED)                          [u_effective = u, in [0,0.5)]
#   U in [0.5,1)   -> texel1 (GREEN)                         [u_effective = u, in [0.5,1)]
#   U in [1,1.5)   -> texel1 (GREEN, MIRRORED continuation)  [u_effective = 2-u, in [0.5,1)]
#   U in [1.5,2)   -> texel0 (RED, mirrored back)            [u_effective = 2-u, in [0,0.5)]
# Expected screen pattern: RED,GREEN,GREEN,RED (symmetric) -- genuinely distinguishable from
# sprite_wrap_quad.scene's own RED,GREEN,RED,GREEN (repeating) pattern using the IDENTICAL source
# data and geometry, isolating the address-mode behavior itself as the only variable.
width=256
height=256
profile=HiDef
clearcolor=100,149,237,255
spritebatchmode=true
texturewidth=2
textureheight=1
texturepixel=255,0,0,255
texturepixel=0,255,0,255
spritedestrect=64,108,128,40
spritesourcerect=0,0,4,1
spritesampler=PointMirror
spritecolor=255,255,255,255
